WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.360
Locate the testis, epididymis, and vas deferens on the

00:00:03.360 --> 00:00:04.513
anatomical illustration.

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:06.692
The testis produces sperm.

00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:10.337
Sperm mature in the epididymis, and the vas deferens

00:00:10.340 --> 00:00:12.151
transports them toward the urethra.

00:00:12.780 --> 00:00:15.253
For epididymitis, reverse that usual direction.

00:00:16.140 --> 00:00:19.780
The supplied slide describes
a microorganism ascending the vas

00:00:19.840 --> 00:00:22.520
deferens from an infected bladder or urethra to reach

00:00:22.520 --> 00:00:23.374
the epididymis.

00:00:23.740 --> 00:00:27.640
Watch the highlighted inflammatory
change develop at the epididymis.

00:00:27.640 --> 00:00:30.526
Epididymitis is inflammation of the epididymis.

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:33.812
Orchitis is infection of the testis and may occur

00:00:33.820 --> 00:00:34.778
with epididymitis.

00:00:35.440 --> 00:00:37.800
Similar pain does not make these the same affected

00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:38.322
structure.

00:00:39.160 --> 00:00:42.043
The epididymitis slide lists pain and the Prehn sign,

00:00:42.060 --> 00:00:46.542
with antibiotics, analgesics, ice,
and scrotal elevation as treatments.

00:00:47.120 --> 00:00:49.920
It does not provide
a complete organism or complication

00:00:49.920 --> 00:00:50.295
list.

00:00:50.740 --> 00:00:53.500
Those textbook details remain marked as gaps in this

00:00:53.500 --> 00:00:53.816
guide.
